From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] lock-tklock: the power key wakes and unlocks in one press

On the Nokia N950 the visual tklock's swipe is unreliable, and a power-key
press only shows the lockscreen, which mce blanks again after five seconds
(DEFAULT_VISUAL_BLANK_DELAY) unless it is swiped away. With PowerKeyUnlocks
(group [PowerKey], default on) the press takes the path of a
req_tklock_mode_change "unlocked" request instead: set_tklock_state(LOCK_OFF)
closes the lockscreen UI, clears the tklock submodes and resumes touch, and
synthesise_activity() keeps the display on. PowerKeyUnlocks=false restores
the lockscreen.

The N950 runs the Maemo stack (10-maemo.ini loads lock-tklock, not
lock-generic), so this is where the power key's tklock handling lives.

Tested on the N950 with KEY_POWER events injected into twl4030_pwrbutton:
display off and tklock locked before, display on and unlocked after, on
every try. A press on the physical button is still to be confirmed.
---
--- a/src/modules/lock-tklock.c
+++ b/src/modules/lock-tklock.c
@@ -157,6 +157,11 @@
 static submode_t call_submode = MCE_INVALID_SUBMODE;
 
 static uint16_t power_keycode;
+/* When set, a power-key press directly wakes and unlocks instead of only
+ * showing the visual tklock UI. The N950's lockscreen swipe is unreliable,
+ * so the power button unlocks in one press. Config: [PowerKey]
+ * PowerKeyUnlocks (default: on). */
+static gboolean powerkey_unlocks = TRUE;
 
 /** TKLock UI state type */
 typedef enum {
@@ -1527,6 +1532,17 @@
 			disable_eveater(TRUE);
 			synthesise_activity();
 		}
+		else if (powerkey_unlocks && is_tklock_enabled()) {
+			/* Power key wakes and unlocks in one press. This is
+			 * the same path as a req_tklock_mode_change "unlocked"
+			 * request: it closes the lockscreen UI, clears the
+			 * tklock submodes and resumes touch, which is reliable
+			 * even when the lockscreen swipe is not. */
+			mce_log(LL_DEBUG, "power key - direct unlock");
+			set_tklock_state(LOCK_OFF);
+			synthesise_activity();
+			update_saved_submode();
+		}
 		else
 			trigger_visual_tklock();
 	}
@@ -2083,6 +2099,8 @@
 
 	power_keycode = mce_conf_get_int(MCE_CONF_POWERKEY_GROUP, MCE_CONF_POWERKEY_KEYCODE, KEY_POWER, NULL);
 
+	powerkey_unlocks = mce_conf_get_bool(MCE_CONF_POWERKEY_GROUP, "PowerKeyUnlocks", TRUE, NULL);
+
 	blank_immediately = mce_conf_get_bool(MCE_CONF_TKLOCK_GROUP,
 					      MCE_CONF_BLANK_IMMEDIATELY,
 					      DEFAULT_BLANK_IMMEDIATELY,
